    "gene": "ACHE",
    "target_id": "ENSG00000087085",
    "evidence_types": [
      "Human clinical intervention: randomized trials summarized in a Cochrane review show small cognitive benefits from the acetylcholinesterase inhibitor donepezil in Alzheimer dementia (PMID:29923184; DOI:10.1002/14651858.CD001190.pub3).",
      "Human postmortem neurochemistry: cortical acetylcholinesterase and choline acetyltransferase activities decreased with increasing plaque counts; reduced choline acetyltransferase correlated with intellectual impairment. This supports cholinergic pathway dysfunction, not ACHE overactivity or genetic causality (PMID:719462; DOI:10.1136/bmj.2.6150.1457)."
    ],
    "direction": "Inhibit acetylcholinesterase activity to prolong synaptic acetylcholine signaling and provide symptomatic cognitive benefit; disease modification is not established, and tolerability limits inhibition."
  },
  {
    "gene": "APP",
    "target_id": "ENSG00000142192",
    "evidence_types": [
      "Human genetics: the APP A673T coding variant protects against Alzheimer disease and age-related cognitive decline and reduces amyloidogenic peptide formation in vitro (PMID:22801501; DOI:10.1038/nature11283).",
      "Human clinical intervention: lecanemab, targeting APP-derived amyloid-beta protofibrils, slowed cognitive and functional decline in biomarker-confirmed early Alzheimer disease; this supports targeting a downstream APP product, not direct inhibition of full-length APP (PMID:36449413; DOI:10.1056/NEJMoa2212948)."
    ],
    "direction": "Hypothesis: selectively reduce pathogenic APP-derived amyloid-beta production or enhance its clearance while preserving physiological APP function. The cited lecanemab trial supports amyloid-beta clearance in early Alzheimer disease; it does not establish cognitive benefit from inhibiting APP expression or amyloidogenic processing. Amyloid-clearing antibodies carry amyloid-related imaging abnormality (ARIA) risk."
